<root id="full-stack" class="flow">
  <div class="flow-head">
    <h2>One language, the whole flow</h2>
    <p>
      Follow one request through the stack — the same Rust types run in
      the browser and on the server. Scroll the steps; the issue tracker
      on the right builds up, goes live, and ships.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="flow-layout">
    <!-- Steps on a timeline; scroll-spy drives the demo's stage -->
    <div class="flow-steps">
      <article class="flow-step" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-55%.0="enter1">
        <span class="flow-step-num" :data-active="active == 1 ? 'true' : 'false'">1</span>
        <div class="flow-step-body">
          <h3>Write a component</h3>
          <p>A <code>.poco</code> template plus a Rust struct — state is just fields, handlers mutate <code>&amp;mut self</code>. No virtual DOM.</p>
          <pre class="flow-code"><code pp-html="code1"></code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="flow-step" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-55%.0="enter2">
        <span class="flow-step-num" :data-active="active == 2 ? 'true' : 'false'">2</span>
        <div class="flow-step-body">
          <h3>Call the server, typed</h3>
          <p>Mark an async fn <code>#[server]</code> and call it from the browser like any async fn — same types, both ends, no fetch glue.</p>
          <pre class="flow-code"><code pp-html="code2"></code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="flow-step" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-55%.0="enter3">
        <span class="flow-step-num" :data-active="active == 3 ? 'true' : 'false'">3</span>
        <div class="flow-step-body">
          <h3>Data is local-first and live</h3>
          <p>A <code>#[query_resource]</code> view reads instantly and updates optimistically; the server pushes each change back to every client.</p>
          <pre class="flow-code"><code pp-html="code3"></code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="flow-step" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-55%.0="enter4">
        <span class="flow-step-num" :data-active="active == 4 ? 'true' : 'false'">4</span>
        <div class="flow-step-body">
          <h3>Auth &amp; services, wired in</h3>
          <p>The request is authenticated by the same model as the client; object storage and Redis-backed jobs are one <code>plugin</code> away.</p>
          <pre class="flow-code"><code pp-html="code4"></code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="flow-step" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-55%.0="enter5">
        <span class="flow-step-num" :data-active="active == 5 ? 'true' : 'false'">5</span>
        <div class="flow-step-body">
          <h3>Observe it, ship it</h3>
          <p>Every hop emits a structured event for logs, traces, and analytics — and the whole thing deploys as one container. Try “Add issue”.</p>
          <pre class="flow-code"><code pp-html="code5"></code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- Sticky interactive preview: builds up, goes live, then ships -->
    <div class="flow-stage">
      <issue-flow-demo :stage="active"></issue-flow-demo>

      <a class="flow-cta" href="/docs/getting-started/introduction" pp-route>
        How it fits together
        <span class="flow-arrow-link">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</root>
